  "human_edit_summary": "Post-implementation provenance re-review (no findings loop). tasks.md was NOT edited and has not changed at all since attempt-6: its raw bytes are still those of commit 472579a3 (2026-08-19), which predates attempt-6's own re-bind commit e081f334 (2026-08-21), and normalized_hash(tasks.md, task) recomputes today to 38770deaf590060af86a7043224e2c202bed13dfb6b84ee21d6e98885abd815c, byte-for-byte the value attempt-6/round-1 pinned. Task statuses stand at T-001/T-002 Done, T-003/T-004/T-005 Implementation Complete, T-006..T-010 Planned -- the same state attempt-6 reviewed. What went stale is the rest of the top-level contract: requirements.md, acceptance-tests.md and design.md were amended under three human rulings dated 2026-08-24 (commits 88c3187a, 2f35de22, 3e0e72cd), which cite 31 previously unnamed acceptance criteria, add the substance of AC-016 and AC-056, correct a stale '14-value enum' claim to sixteen, and repair two dangling 'Edge Cases below' pointers. AC-035/AC-036/AC-037 remain deliberately uncited as Global-scoped registration-commit meta-criteria. This attempt re-binds the attempt-6/round-1 clean PASS to the amended hashes. tasks_sha256 deliberately carries the flip-invariant normalized form rather than the precheck's raw bytes (ea82d6f08a8c82de38f15cc76c4cc6d6702651232210bf20640ac3dd68cf7d25), so that T-003..T-010's remaining lifecycle transitions cannot re-stale this record; check-workflow-state.sh's reviewed_hash_accepted() admits either form. Both reviewer manifests carry the raw bytes, which is what each reviewer actually verified on disk.",
